  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-82378",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Since the period is $5,$ if we add (or subtract) any multiple of $5$ from the input, the output stays the same.\n\nSo, we can keep subtracting $5$ from the input until we get to an input that we see in the graph:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(132) & =f(132-5) \\\\  & =f(132-2\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =⋯ \\\\  & =f(132-26\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =f(2) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
